    <section
      class="feature-grid"
      id="features"
      aria-label="Loomey features"
    >
      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Reading Home</p>

        <h3>See the parts of your reading life that matter right now</h3>

        <p>
          Loomey's Home experience brings current reading context together so you
          can return to books, progress, goals, and active reading without digging
          through the rest of the app first. It acts as the front door to the
          reading system rather than a disconnected summary screen.
        </p>

        <div class="chip-row">
          <span>Current Reading</span>
          <span>Reading Momentum</span>
          <span>Goals</span>
          <span>Progress</span>
          <span>Quick Access</span>
          <span>Theme-Aware UI</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Books & Library</p>

        <h3>Keep your collection organized around the books you actually read</h3>

        <p>
          Loomey's Books area gives your reading collection its own dedicated
          library with detailed book records and navigation into the rest of each
          book's reading data. Search and browse your books, open individual
          details, and keep the library connected to sessions, goals, notes, and
          progress instead of treating a title as a static catalog entry.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Goals</p>

        <h3>Track reading goals in the form that fits what you are trying to accomplish</h3>

        <p>
          Loomey includes a dedicated Goals system for recurring and one-time
          reading targets, with goal history kept separately for reviewing what
          happened over time. Goals can stay connected to the books and reading
          activity they measure rather than living as generic checkboxes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Stats & History</p>

        <h3>Look back at how you read instead of only where you stopped</h3>

        <p>
          Reading statistics are built from real session data and give Loomey a
          dedicated place for understanding progress beyond a single book. Goal
          History preserves past goal activity separately, while session history,
          streak logic, and progress records make it possible to see patterns in
          the reading you have already done.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">EPUB Library</p>

        <h3>Keep imported EPUB books available inside the same reading environment</h3>

        <p>
          Loomey includes a dedicated EPUB Library with document-import support,
          giving digital books their own place inside the app instead of separating
          imported reading from the rest of your library. EPUB reading remains
          connected to the same account and reading environment as your other books.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Sprints, Buddies, Bingos & Challenges</p>

        <h3>Give reading social, focused, and playful spaces without disconnecting it from progress</h3>

        <p>
          Loomey includes focused Sprint rooms, Buddy Reading, Reading Bingos, and
          Challenges as dedicated reading experiences. These areas add structure,
          shared participation, and variety around reading while remaining part of
          the same app that tracks your books, goals, sessions, and statistics.
        </p>

        <div class="reader-preview">
          <div class="reader-preview-top">
            <span>Reading Experiences</span>
            <strong>Connected</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-bar">
            <span></span>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-meta">
            <span>Sprints</span>
            <span>Buddies</span>
            <span>Bingos</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="spotlight reveal">
      <div class="spotlight-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">More Than a Book List</p>

        <h2>Reading becomes more useful to track when the context around each book stays attached</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey is built to keep books connected to the way you actually read
          them: sessions, goals, streaks, statistics, history, notes, sprints,
          community features, and digital reading all have their own places while
          still belonging to the same reading life.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="share-demo" aria-label="Loomey reading preview">
        <span class="share-pill">Reading Context</span>

        <h4>Keep the book and everything around it together.</h4>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Sessions</span>
          <strong>Record the reading you actually complete</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Goals</span>
          <strong>Track progress in the form that fits the target</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Stats</span>
          <strong>Look back at patterns across your reading history</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-section reveal">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Everything Else</p>

        <h2>Open each part of the Loomey experience</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="details-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Reading Sessions & Progress</b>
              <small>Keep actual reading activity attached to books and long-term progress</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Loomey's reading system records sessions as their own data instead of
            reducing progress to a manually edited number. That session history
            feeds the broader reading experience, including stats, streaks, goals,
            and the progress shown across the app.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Reading Goals & Goal History</b>
              <small>Set targets now and preserve what happened after they change or finish</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Goals have their own primary area while Goal History provides a
            separate place for reviewing past goal activity. This keeps active
            targets focused on what you are working toward now without erasing
            previous progress once a goal changes state.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Reading Stats & Streaks</b>
              <small>Use session data to understand momentum and consistency over time</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The Stats area works from stored reading sessions and provides a
            dedicated view into how your reading is accumulating. Streak and
            momentum-related logic gives consistency its own place instead of
            making the current book the only measure of progress.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Reading Bingos</b>
              <small>Turn themed reading prompts into board-style progress you can revisit</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Reading Bingos have their own hub and persistent progress records,
            allowing board completion to remain part of Loomey's reading data
            rather than disappearing when you leave the screen.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Reading Sprints & Buddy Reading</b>
              <small>Read with focus or alongside other readers without leaving your main reading system</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Loomey includes a dedicated Sprint Room for focused reading sessions
            and Buddy Reading for shared reading experiences. Both live beside
            your core library, stats, goals, and history rather than operating as
            disconnected extras.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>EPUB Import & Digital Library</b>
              <small>Bring EPUB files into a dedicated in-app library</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The EPUB Library uses document-import support so EPUB files can be
            added directly into Loomey and kept in their own digital-reading area.
            This gives imported books a home inside the same app as the rest of
            your reading collection.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Profile, Themes & Settings</b>
              <small>Keep your reading identity and interface preferences attached to the same app</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Loomey includes dedicated Profile and Settings areas alongside a
            theme controller that updates the appearance of the main reading
            interface and navigation. The reading experience can keep its visual
            identity while your account-facing information and preferences remain
            available from the same app.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="community-banner reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built Around the Way Reading Actually Grows</p>

        <h2>A reading life is made from books, time, goals, memory, progress, and the people you share it with.</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey gives each of those pieces its own space without breaking them
          apart. Your library, sessions, statistics, goals, history, EPUBs,
          sprints, buddies, bingos, challenges, profile, and settings all remain
          different parts of one connected reading companion.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="primary-button raised-button" href="https://discord.gg/SaZJKF3d9U">
        Join the Community
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Loomey</p>

      <h2>Keep your books, progress, goals, stats, and reading experiences connected in one place.</h2>

      <p>
        Learn more about Loomey, report a problem, share an idea, or reach out
        directly through Voxiverse Support.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-grid">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/asteriasmoons/Loomey/issues/1"
          class="cta-card"
        >
          <span class="cta-kicker">Report an Issue</span>

          <h2>Loomey Bug Reports</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open Reports</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/github" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Ideas & Discussions</span>

          <h2>Voxiverse on GitHub</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open GitHub</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Need Help?</span>

          <h2>Contact Support</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Get Support</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<script>
  const revealItems = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");

  const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.12 }
  );

  revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));

  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-loomey-gallery]")
    .forEach((gallery) => {
      const track =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-track]");

      const slides = Array.from(
        gallery.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".gallery-slide")
      );

      const previousButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-previous]"
        );

      const nextButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-next]"
        );

      const count =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-count]");

      const progress =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-progress]");

      if (
        !track ||
        !slides.length ||
        !previousButton ||
        !nextButton
      ) {
        return;
      }

      let currentIndex = 0;
      let autoplay: number | undefined;
      let dragStartX = 0;

      const updateGallery = () => {
        track.style.transform =
          `translateX(-${currentIndex * 100}%)`;

        slides.forEach((slide, index) => {
          slide.classList.toggle(
            "is-active",
            index === currentIndex
          );
        });

        if (count) {
          count.textContent =
            `${currentIndex + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
        }

        if (progress) {
          progress.style.width =
            `${((currentIndex + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
        }
      };

      const showSlide = (index: number) => {
        currentIndex =
          (index + slides.length) % slides.length;

        updateGallery();
      };

      const startAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);

        autoplay = window.setInterval(
          () => showSlide(currentIndex + 1),
          4200
        );
      };

      const stopAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);
      };

      nextButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex + 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      previousButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex - 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
        dragStartX = event.clientX;
        stopAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerup", (event) => {
        const deltaX = event.clientX - dragStartX;

        if (Math.abs(deltaX) > 40) {
          showSlide(
            currentIndex + (deltaX < 0 ? 1 : -1)
          );
        }

        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseenter",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseleave",
        startAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusin",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusout",
        startAutoplay
      );

      window.addEventListener(
        "resize",
        updateGallery
      );

      updateGallery();
      startAutoplay();
    });
</script>

<style>
  .loomey-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 1rem 0 5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(0, 1.2fr)
      minmax(310px, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    min-height: 620px;
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .hero-copy,
  .hero-showcase {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .card-kicker,
  .mini-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .hero-text,
  .intro-section p,
  .spotlight p,
  .community-banner p,
  .cta-section > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-button,
  .secondary-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 50px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .primary-button {
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .secondary-button {
    background: var(--surface-raised) !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }

  .primary-button:hover,
  .secondary-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .hero-showcase {
    min-height: 410px;
  }

  .showcase-card,
  .floating-card,
  .feature-card,
  .share-demo,
  .details-list details,
  .community-banner,
  .cta-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow-soft);
  }

  .main-card {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 55px 20px 55px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 30px;
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }

  .main-card h4 {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .progress-line {
    height: 10px;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-line span {
    display: block;
    width: 72%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    animation: pulse-width 3s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .showcase-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .showcase-stats b {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

